# Free LLM providers — generated from registry.yaml, do not edit by hand.
# Fill the keys you use, then `source` this file. Every endpoint is
# OpenAI-compatible: point any SDK/agent at the base URL next to the key.

# ── Google AI Studio (Gemini API) — base: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/ · get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
export GOOGLE_AI_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: pass the key as Bearer

# ── opencode — no key needed · base: https://opencode.ai/zen/v1
#    header: every request needs a stable id per conversation in x-opencode-session — send it from your client
#    note: no key needed for the free ids as long as every request carries a stable id per conversation in x-opencode-session; ling-3.0-flash-fin-free answered keyless three times out of three on 2026-09-16 while big-pickle and mimo-v2.5-free answered 429 FreeUsageLimitError every time. Clients send the header themselves, so the generated LiteLLM and opencode configs leave this row out; inside OpenCode the ids are `opencode/<model-id>`. muse-spark-1.3-contributor-free is served on /v1/responses only

# ── OpenRouter (free models) — base: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 · get a key: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: pick models with the :free suffix: every id carrying it is priced 0/0, twenty on 2026-09-16, and the lane rotates, so a new id waits two weeks for the Models column. Six are not coding models: openrouter/free is the free-models router, nemotron-3.5-content-safety a guardrail, ling-3.0-flash-fin and ling-3.0-flash-sante finance- and health-tuned, nemotron-3-nano-omni a perception sub-agent, and LiquidAI warns lfm-2.5-2.6b off agentic coding. For Claude Code, OpenRouter's cookbook sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to https://openrouter.ai/api with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty and a :free id as ANTHROPIC_MODEL

# ── Groq — base: https://api.groq.com/openai/v1 · get a key: https://console.groq.com/keys
export GROQ_API_KEY=""
#    note: the chat models Groq's own Free Plan Limits table names; its safeguard and prompt-guard classifiers, compound systems, whisper and orpheus rows are left out

# ── Kilo Code — no key needed · base: https://api.kilo.ai/api/gateway
#    note: no key at all for the free ids, capped at 200 requests per hour per IP; a metered id answers 401 `You need to sign in to use this model`. Every id listed is one the catalog marks isFree and mayTrainOnYourPrompts. kilo-auto/free leads because it routes over the free models the catalog's autoRouting list names; it and openrouter/free are routers and nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier, so none of the three is a coding model

# ── Requesty — base: https://router.requesty.ai/v1 · get a key: https://app.requesty.ai/api-keys
export REQUESTY_API_KEY=""
#    note: the twelve ids listed are every row the catalog prices at 0, and the free plan serves those alone; ids carry no :free suffix, so the price is the only thing separating them from the metered rows. Every NVIDIA and Poolside row is marked data_used_for_training with 30-day retention, and nemotron-3.5-content-safety is a guardrail classifier. For Claude Code, the guide sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to https://router.requesty.ai (router.eu.requesty.ai for EU residency)

# ── AIHubMix (free models) — base: https://aihubmix.com/v1 · get a key: https://aihubmix.com/token
export AIHUBMIX_API_KEY=""
#    note: every id the catalog prices at 0 is listed or ignored on purpose, 60 rows on 2026-09-17; free ids carry a -free suffix beside a metered twin. ox-alpha is a codename the catalog resolves: "This model actually points to glm-5.3-flash". Ignored: gpt-image-2-free and gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview-free generate images, qwen3.6-plus-preview-free says it was "removed from the platform", and gpt-live-transcribe is speech-to-text. For Claude Code, ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL is https://aihubmix.com, as its Claude Code guide sets it

# ── Z.ai (Zhipu GLM) — base: https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4 · get a key: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
export ZAI_GLM_API_KEY=""
#    note: Coding-Plan keys use https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4 instead. The Claude Code guide sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL to https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic with "your_zai_api_key" as the token and names Coding-Plan ids (glm-5.3, glm-5.3-flash); whether the free Flash ids answer on that route is not stated, and the route answers 401 keyless (2026-09-05)

# ── Cloudflare Workers AI — base: https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/ai/v1 · get a key: https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens
export CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: substitute {account_id} with your Cloudflare account ID

# ── Routeway — base: https://api.routeway.ai/v1 · get a key: https://routeway.ai/dashboard/keys
export ROUTEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: the three :free ids are every zero-priced row in the catalog on 2026-09-16, all marked available; only the :free suffix is free, and the same catalog meters Claude and GPT at list rates. An id joins the Models column only after two weeks in the lane, since every family there is re-checked on every run and three misses archive the row

# ── LLM7.io — no key needed · base: https://api.llm7.io/v1
#    note: no key for the anonymous tier — OpenAI SDKs want some api_key, and the quickstart passes `unused`. The ids listed are the turbo rows that answered a keyless call on 2026-09-16; DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731 and gemini-3.1-flash-lite need a token

# ── LLMTR — base: https://llmtr.com/v1 · get a key: https://llmtr.com/dashboard/api-keys
export LLMTR_API_KEY=""
#    note: the thirteen ids are every chat row the public catalog prices at 0 on 2026-09-16, motif/motif-3 created that evening. qwen/qwen3.8-flash-free, inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-vl and inclusionai/ling-3.0-flash-sante are free only until 22 September 2026, and dots-studio/dots-3-note-preview closes on 30 September 2026. nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b is the free daily-quota row and its -262k twin the metered one; openai/gpt-oss-safeguard-20b is a content classifier rather than a coding model. liquid/lfm-2.5-embedding-350m-free is ignored as an embeddings row

# ── SambaNova Cloud — base: https://api.sambanova.ai/v1 · get a key: https://cloud.sambanova.ai/apis
export SAMBANOVA_CLOUD_API_KEY=""
#    note: model ids are case-sensitive; the catalog publishes list prices for every row, so the free tier is a quota rather than a zero-priced lane

# ── Vercel AI Gateway — base: https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1 · get a key: https://vercel.com/dashboard/ai-gateway/api-keys
export VERCEL_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""
#    note: every id listed is priced 0 in and 0 out and draws nothing from the $5 credit; any other Free-Tier-eligible model spends it. Zero-priced ids come and go within days, so a new one waits two weeks for the Models column. spacexai/grok-stt also shows a zero but is speech-to-text billed per second of audio. The same key serves the Anthropic Messages format at https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh, which Vercel's docs give as Claude Code's ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty

# ── Hetzner Inference API — base: https://inference.hetzner.com/api/v1 · get a key: https://experiments.hetzner.com/inference
export HETZNER_INFERENCE_API_KEY=""
#    note: both ids are 262K-context and take text and images; /v1/models, /v1/completions and /v1/chat/completions are the whole surface. The key is minted in the Inference tab of experiments.hetzner.com, which is a client-rendered page behind a Hetzner login — the readable copy of the terms is the docs page this row probes

# ── Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (DashScope, international) — base: https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1 · get a key: https://modelstudio.console.alibabacloud.com
export ALIBABA_MODEL_STUDIO_API_KEY=""
#    note: international (Singapore) endpoint; keys are region-specific

# ── BazaarLink — base: https://api.bazaarlink.ai/v1 · get a key: https://bazaarlink.ai/keys
export BAZAARLINK_API_KEY=""
#    note: only the two :free ids and auto:free cost nothing — the plain qwen3.7-flash beside the first is the metered twin ($0.03/$0.13 per 1M), and deepseek-v4-flash-0731free without the suffix is metered at $0.20/$0.40. auto:free picks a free model for you, and on a funded account it can fall through to the paid routing table "unless paid fallback is disabled"

# ── Nous Portal (Hermes Agent) — base: https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1 · get a key: https://portal.nousresearch.com
export NOUS_PORTAL_API_KEY=""
#    note: every id the keyless catalog prices at 0 on 2026-09-16; stealth/union-alpha is a stealth model without the :free suffix, and solar-pro4 is a limited-time trial on other gateways

# ── NVIDIA NIM (build.nvidia.com) — base: https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1 · get a key: https://build.nvidia.com
export NVIDIA_NIM_API_KEY=""
#    note: the catalog endpoint answers unauthenticated, which is what the probe reads — it confirms NVIDIA still hosts these models, not that your account still has credits to call them with, and it publishes no price field at all, so hosting is the only question it can answer

# ── TokenRouter (PaleBlueDot) — base: https://api.tokenrouter.com/v1 · get a key: https://www.tokenrouter.com/console/token
export TOKENROUTER_API_KEY=""
#    note: one id in the catalog is priced 0 under the free marker, and it is the whole free lane here — nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning:free, alone on 2026-08-14 and again on 2026-09-16; z-ai/glm-5.3-free stood beside it from 2026-09-02 until it left the catalog between the 2026-09-14 and 2026-09-16 reads. PaleBlueDot AI runs this gateway on tokenrouter.com; same-name gateways on other TLDs are separate services and their keys do not work here

# ── Cohere (trial keys) — base: https://api.cohere.com/compatibility/v1 · get a key: https://dashboard.cohere.com/api-keys
export COHERE_API_KEY=""
#    note: OpenAI-compatible endpoint; native API lives at https://api.cohere.com/v2. Both ids are the Model ID Cohere's own model pages publish — north-mini-code-1-0 is the free-on-any-key one

# ── Regolo AI — base: https://api.regolo.ai/v1 · get a key: https://dashboard.regolo.ai
export REGOLO_API_KEY=""
#    note: GET /v1/models is public and needs no key, but it publishes ids only — the prices and the trial terms are on the pricing page this row probes. brick-v1-beta is the one id priced at zero on that page

# ── Token Harbor — base: https://tokenharbor.ai/v1 · get a key: https://tokenharbor.ai/dashboard/api-keys
export TOKEN_HARBOR_API_KEY=""
#    note: the :free suffix selects the free route, which has to be switched on in the dashboard first; /v1/models needs a key, so the ids are the free rows the models page publishes (2026-09-16)

# ── Mistral AI Studio — base: https://api.mistral.ai/v1 · get a key: https://console.mistral.ai/api-keys
export MISTRAL_API_KEY=""
#    note: Free mode is on by default for a new account; create the key under Studio › API Keys. A key made under Code › Vibe CLI is a plan key that spends the plan's Vibe budget, which Mistral tells API users to avoid

# ── VLM Run Gateway — no key needed · base: https://gateway.vlm.run/v1/openai
#    note: no key: a call with no Authorization header is anonymous, and `Bearer vlmrun` is the explicit anonymous form for a client that needs a non-empty key; 10 a minute, 30 an hour and 100 a day per IP. qwen/qwen3.5-0.8b is the other chat model on VLM Run's GPUs, and the routed ids in the same catalog, Kimi K3 among them, answer `403 model_not_entitled` without a paid organization

# ── Hugging Face Inference Providers — base: https://router.huggingface.co/v1 · get a key: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
export HUGGINGFACE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=""
#    note: chat-only; model ids namespaced (openai/gpt-oss-120b)

# ── OVHcloud AI Endpoints — no key needed · base: https://oai.endpoints.kepler.ai.cloud.ovh.net/v1
#    note: no key at all on the anonymous lane, which OVHcloud rate-limits at 2 requests per minute per IP per model — a 429 means wait about half a minute, not that the offer is gone. An API access key from a Public Cloud project raises that to 400 per minute and bills per token from then on, except on Qwen3.8-27B, which the catalog prices at zero

# ── Upstage (Solar API) — base: https://api.upstage.ai/v1 · get a key: https://console.upstage.ai/api-keys
export UPSTAGE_API_KEY=""

# ── MegaNova — base: https://api.meganova.ai/v1 · get a key: https://www.meganova.ai/api-keys
export MEGANOVA_API_KEY=""
#    note: the three ids listed are the chat rows a Tier 1 account can call for free; ten more zero-priced rows are ignored on purpose — zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash and manta-pro-1.0 have a Tier 1 quota of 0, faster-whisper, Qwen3-Embedding-8B and bge-reranker-v2-m3 are not chat models, and five are roleplay fine-tunes (four of Llama, one of Mistral NeMo). Manta Mini and Manta Flash are MegaNova's own routers, tagged best_role_play in the catalog, so Mistral Small 3.2, at 8,192 tokens of context, is the one named coding model on the lane

# ── SEA-LION (AI Singapore) — base: https://api.sea-lion.ai/v1 · get a key: https://playground.sea-lion.ai/key-manager
export SEA_LION_API_KEY=""
#    note: the key manager calls it a Trial API Key but publishes no expiry and no credit balance — the documented ceiling is the 10 calls/min rate limit. /v1/models needs the key, so the probe reads the offer page

# ── OpenTyphoon (SCB 10X) — base: https://api.opentyphoon.ai/v1 · get a key: https://playground.opentyphoon.ai/api-key
export OPENTYPHOON_API_KEY=""
#    note: the one chat id in the keyless catalog on 2026-09-05; the other five rows are OCR (typhoon-ocr, typhoon-ocr-v1.5, typhoon-ocr-preview) and speech (typhoon-asr-realtime, typhoon-isan-asr-realtime). Typhoon 2.5 is a Qwen3-30B-A3B fine-tune for Thai, so it is a Qwen-class coder that also reads Thai; the Free models column stays empty because the FAQ the probe reads names no model

# ── Agnes AI — base: https://apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1 · get a key: https://platform.agnes-ai.com
export AGNES_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: the quickstart sends its chat completion to apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1/chat/completions with a Bearer key from the Agnes AI Platform dashboard; free and Token Plan keys draw on separate limit pools, and creating more keys of one type does not stack RPM

# ── Sarvam AI — base: https://api.sarvam.ai/v1 · get a key: https://dashboard.sarvam.ai
export SARVAM_API_KEY=""
#    note: the vendor's own header is api-subscription-key, and the same key is accepted as "Authorization: Bearer" on every endpoint. /v1/chat/completions serves only sarvam-105b and sarvam-105b-conversations; the open models are on the /v2 beta, whitelisted per key. Prices are in rupees

# ── SenseNova (SenseTime 商汤) — base: https://token.sensenova.cn/v1 · get a key: https://platform.sensenova.cn
export SENSENOVA_API_KEY=""
#    note: the base url is not printed on any server-rendered page — it is taken from the vendor's console docs and corroborated directly, since token.sensenova.cn/v1/models answers 401 `Authorization Not Found` in an OpenAI-shaped envelope. The callable ids live only in that JavaScript console, which no probe here can read, so none are published; the plan page names "SenseNova 6.8 Flash Lite" in prose alone.

# ── Tencent Cloud TokenHub — base: https://tokenhub.tencentmaas.com/v1 · get a key: https://console.cloud.tencent.com/tokenhub/apikey
export TENCENT_TOKENHUB_API_KEY=""
#    note: ids are the models page's model column (调用参数), read 2026-09-17; /v1/models answers 401 without a key, so none is read off a catalog. The Claude Code guide sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://tokenhub.tencentmaas.com with ANTHROPIC_MODEL=hy3

# ── Inception Labs (Mercury) — base: https://api.inceptionlabs.ai/v1 · get a key: https://platform.inceptionlabs.ai
export INCEPTION_LABS_API_KEY=""
#    note: mercury-2.5 and mercury-2 answer /v1/chat/completions and are the two ids /v1/models lists; mercury-edit-2 answers /v1/fim/completions and /v1/edit/completions instead and is absent from that catalog by design, so an OpenAI-shaped chat client cannot call it — point an autocomplete plugin at it, not a chat agent

# ── Pollinations.AI — no key needed · base: https://text.pollinations.ai/openai
#    note: anonymous works and needs no key. The optional token that raises the rate limit has no working signup — auth.pollinations.ai, the host the vendor's own APIDOCS still sends you to, stopped resolving (NXDOMAIN from both Cloudflare and Google resolvers, 2026-08-14)

# ── FreeInference (Harvard SEAS) — base: https://freeinference.org/v1 · get a key: https://freeinference.org
export FREEINFERENCE_API_KEY=""
#    note: the three ids are the chat rows the keyless catalog at freeinference.org/v1/models returned on 2026-09-05 (bge-m3, the fourth, is an embedding model); the docs mark four more chat ids Free, which stay out of the generated configs until a keyed read confirms them. The catalog's prices are upstream reference accounting, "not fees charged by FreeInference to users". The same key serves https://freeinference.org/anthropic, which the docs give as Claude Code's ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL

# ── Fireworks AI — base: https://api.fireworks.ai/inference/v1 · get a key: https://app.fireworks.ai/settings/users/api-keys
export FIREWORKS_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: ids are accounts/fireworks/models/ plus the slug the serverless pricing page links, read 2026-09-17; /inference/v1/models answers 401 without a key, so none is read off a catalog. The quickstart gives the Anthropic SDK base_url https://api.fireworks.ai/inference, which is Claude Code's ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, the client appending /v1/messages

# ── Ollama Cloud — base: https://ollama.com/v1 · get a key: https://ollama.com/settings/keys
export OLLAMA_CLOUD_API_KEY=""
#    note: the three ids left are the ones a key on the $0 plan actually answered on 2026-09-02, in that order of speed; minimax-m3 was dropped from this list because the same key gets 402 Payment Required for it. Which models the starter credits reach is published nowhere, so this list is measured rather than read, and /v1/models still lists the whole catalog, starter and metered alike

# ── RouterPlex — base: https://api.routerplex.com/v1 · get a key: https://routerplex.com/sign-up
export ROUTERPLEX_API_KEY=""
#    note: ids are the catalog page's own spellings (routerplex.com/models, 54 chat ids on 2026-09-11); the vendor's Claude Code page sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.routerplex.com and ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-6 (guide reviewed 2026-09-13), the Anthropic SDK appending /v1/messages itself. /v1/models is keyed, so none of these ids is checked against a catalog, and which of them the promotional credit can call is not published

# ── Standard Compute — base: https://api.stdcmpt.com/v1 · get a key: https://standardcompute.com/signup
export STANDARDCOMPUTE_API_KEY=""
#    note: one key, two wires: https://api.stdcmpt.com/v1 for OpenAI-shaped clients and https://api.stdcmpt.com for Claude Code — "For Claude Code, use https://api.stdcmpt.com without /v1". /v1/models is keyless and lists the pool the router picks from, 40 unpriced ids on 2026-09-07 with Claude, GPT and Grok among them; requests are smart-routed across it unless a call pins one id. The two ids here are the router's own

# ── Poolside Platform — base: https://inference.poolside.ai/v1 · get a key: https://platform.poolside.ai
export POOLSIDE_API_KEY=""
#    note: the two ids come from docs.poolside.ai/api/overview, a different page from the one the probe reads — the vendor documents no free-versus-paid split for Platform keys anywhere, so this row claims no free models and names none in its column. The key is created by signing in to Poolside Platform, whose dashboard sits behind a Cloudflare check no probe can read

# ── uncloseai (unturf) — no key needed · base: https://hermes.ai.unturf.com/v1
#    note: anonymous: the catalog and chat/completions both answer with no Authorization header at all. One id is served at a time and it rotates — the endpoint is named after Hermes and serves a Qwen build today — so treat the id as this week's, not the offer

# ── Arli AI — base: https://api.arliai.com/v1 · get a key: https://www.arliai.com/account
export ARLI_AI_API_KEY=""
#    note: the quick-start calls it a drop-in OpenAI-API compatible endpoint and uses a placeholder model id; the catalog's names are the models page's, and the coding quick-start connects Roo Code and Kilo Code with a context window set to the model picked. /v1/chat/completions answers 401 without a key

# ── Bytez — base: https://api.bytez.com/models/v2/openai/v1 · get a key: https://bytez.com/api
export BYTEZ_API_KEY=""
#    note: model ids are Hugging Face ids, Qwen/Qwen3-4B being the docs' example; the OpenAI SDK examples pass the key as the api key and the docs' curl sends it bare in Authorization. /v1/models answers 401 without a key, and closed-source models need a provider key of your own

# ── Yolo-Auto — base: https://yolo-auto.com/v1 · get a key: https://yolo-auto.com/app
export YOLO_AUTO_API_KEY=""
#    note: qwen3.8-flash is the one id the Free plan serves, "the recommended model for coding, text, and tool use" in the docs; qwen3.8-27b, the id this row carried until 2026-09-16, is still accepted from clients already configured with it, and yolo is a paid-only route whose server-side target can change. /v1/models and /v1/usage answer 401 without a key, and the free plan's context is 128K where Pro's is 256K

